# Stack: Hono Baller backend (v2)

> Supersedes FastAPI stack (ADR-0011). **`api/` not built yet** — interim stack is `backend/` (FastAPI). This rule defines target conventions.

## Layout (planned)

- `api/src/index.ts` — Hono app, CORS, route mounting
- `api/src/routes/` — `auth`, `courts`, `profiles`, `uploads`
- `api/src/db/` — Drizzle schema + client
- `api/drizzle/` — SQL migrations
- `docker-compose.yml` (repo root) — `db` (PostGIS) + `api` (FastAPI interim until `api/`)

## Local (when scaffolded)

```powershell
copy api\.env.example api\.env
# Fill from backups/env/backend.env.v1 — see docs/deploy/env-migration.md
docker compose up -d --build
```

Health: `GET /health`

## Env (production)

- `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`, `ENVIRONMENT`, `CORS_ORIGINS`
- `B2_KEY_ID`, `B2_APP_KEY`, `B2_BUCKET`, `B2_ENDPOINT`, `B2_REGION` — **Backblaze B2 only**
- `RESEND_API_KEY`, `RESEND_FROM`

## Auth

- Argon2id password hashing
- JWT access + refresh via `jose`
- Email verification + password reset via **Resend**

## Uploads

- `POST /uploads/presign` — B2 S3-compatible presigned PUT

## Flutter

```text
--dart-define=API_BASE_URL=https://api.ballup.net
```

Repository pattern (ADR-0008) — no Supabase client in new code.

## Not in this stack

- Supabase Auth / RLS / Realtime
- MinIO or non-B2 object storage
- FastAPI / Python backend (v1 archived)
